From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not unmount a volume after failing to mount it

The cached MountPoints property may lag behind an external mount.
If Mount then returns AlreadyMounted, unmounting destroys that external
mount. Only the successful Mount path establishes locker ownership.
Preserve the original mount error without attempting unowned cleanup.

Assisted-by: gpt-6-astra via Codex

--- a/libfwupdplugin/fu-volume-locker.c
+++ b/libfwupdplugin/fu-volume-locker.c
@@ -116,16 +116,8 @@
 		return g_steal_pointer(&self);
 
 	/* open volume */
-	if (!fu_volume_mount(volume, error)) {
-		g_autoptr(GError) error_local = NULL;
-		if (!fu_volume_unmount(volume, &error_local)) {
-			if (!g_error_matches(error_local, FWUPD_ERROR, FWUPD_ERROR_NOTHING_TO_DO)) {
-				g_debug("ignoring unmount error on aborted mount: %s",
-					error_local->message);
-			}
-		}
+	if (!fu_volume_mount(volume, error))
 		return NULL;
-	}
 
 	/* success */
 	self->is_open = TRUE;
